# PAM configuration for xlogin's automatic login
# Used only when /etc/xlogin.conf names a user in XLOGIN_AUTOLOGIN, and only
# once per boot. That user turned automatic login on from the login screen,
# AFTER logging in with their password through the xlogin stack.
#
# The ONLY difference from the xlogin stack is the auth line: no password is
# asked for. pam_permit and pam_unix both come from libpam-modules. Account
# checks still run, so an expired or locked account is refused here exactly as
# it would be at the password prompt. The session lines are unchanged, so the
# realtime limits (pam_limits) and seat registration (pam_elogind) still apply.
auth     required    pam_permit.so
account  required    pam_unix.so
session  required    pam_unix.so
session  optional    pam_limits.so
session  optional    pam_elogind.so
